WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:06.487
SQL logic has three possible results TRUE FALSE and
UNKNOWN TRUE

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.875
means the condition is satisfied FALSE means the
condition is not satisfied

00:00:12.777 --> 00:00:16.450
UNKNOWN means SQL does not have enough information
to determine whether the

00:00:16.476 --> 00:00:21.282
condition is true or false This usually happens
because a null value

00:00:21.295 --> 00:00:26.185
is involved The most important rule on this slide is
about the

00:00:26.211 --> 00:00:30.929
WHERE clause A WHERE clause keeps only rows where
the condition evaluates

00:00:30.942 --> 00:00:35.194
to TRUE Rows that evaluate to FALSE are removed but
rows that

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.942
evaluate to UNKNOWN are also removed That behavior
explains many surprising results

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.875
when we start working with missing data
